•	Compositing and Layering: Artists use greenscreen photography (0:36 - 0:50) to isolate actors and objects. These layers are then digitally composited, which involves adding shadows, reflections, and light interactions to ensure the CGI characters feel grounded in their environment rather than floating on top of it.
•	Lighting and Environment Matching: To sell the illusion, the lighting in the digital environment must perfectly match the real-world lighting of the live-action footage (0:36 - 1:17). This includes recreating textures, motion blur, and color grading that mirror the camera settings used on set.
